# Guide
MeliGuideIntro=These steps are done once, in this order. Until step 7 the module only reads: it changes nothing in your listings.
MeliGuideStep=Step
MeliGuideGoThere=Go to the page
MeliGuideByYou=done by you
MeliGuideDone=Done
MeliGuideToDo=To do
MeliGuideStepSku=Put the SKU on every listing
MeliGuideStepSkuText=On Mercado Libre, fill the "SKU" field of every listing (and every variation: size, colour...) with the exact ref of the product in Dolibarr.\nThat is how the module knows which product each listing sells. A listing without a SKU, or whose SKU does not exist in Dolibarr, stays unlinked and its stock is left alone.
MeliGuideStepApp=Create the application at Mercado Libre
MeliGuideStepAppText=Log in to developers.mercadolibre.com.ar with the business account and create an application ("My applications"; menu names may change).\n- Redirect URI: copy the "Return address" from the Settings tab.\n- Scopes: read, write and offline access (offline_access).\n- Notifications: copy the "Notifications address" and tick the topics Orders (orders_v2), Items and Shipments.\nOnce saved, Mercado Libre shows the "App ID" and the "Secret Key": copy them into the Settings tab.
MeliGuideStepConnect=Connect the account
MeliGuideStepConnectText=In the Settings tab, press "Connect to Mercado Libre" and accept with the business account. If Mercado Libre drops the connection (password change, four months unused), the page says so and you connect again the same way.
MeliGuideStepSettings=Fill in the settings
MeliGuideStepSettingsText=Choose:\n- the Dolibarr user sales are recorded with (preferably a dedicated one, e.g. "mercadolibre", allowed to create orders and invoices);\n- the warehouses whose stock is offered on Mercado Libre;\n- the bank account where what Mercado Libre collects is recorded (usually the Mercado Pago one);\n- the "Shipping" service for what the buyer pays for shipping.\nMercado Libre sales are invoiced by themselves: order, invoice and payment. With the ARCA module, the invoice asks for its CAE like any other.
MeliGuideStepLinks=Check the listings
MeliGuideStepLinksText=Press "Read listings" (in Settings) and look at the unlinked ones in the Listings tab: fix the SKU on Mercado Libre, or type the product ref by hand. Mark as ignored those the module must not touch.
MeliGuideStepBuffer=Decide each product's buffer
MeliGuideStepBufferText=The buffer is units not offered on Mercado Libre although in stock. For unique pieces also sold in the shop or online, a buffer of 0 offers the last unit on every channel at once: if it sells in two places in the same minute, one sale is "oversold" and must be cancelled. With a buffer of 1, Mercado Libre does not offer the last unit.\nThere is a general buffer in Settings and one per listing in the Listings tab. It is your decision, product by product.
MeliGuideStepPush=Switch the stock push on
MeliGuideStepPushText=Once the listings are linked correctly, set "Send stock to Mercado Libre" to Yes. From then on, every stock movement in Dolibarr changes the quantity on Mercado Libre within a minute or two, and everything is sent again every night.
MeliGuideStepDaily=Every day: look at the Sales tab
MeliGuideStepDailyText=Sales that need a person come first: oversold, with an unknown product, or cancelled on Mercado Libre after being invoiced (those need a credit note, made by hand). The shipping label is downloaded from there too.

